00:46:46.580 --> 00:46:48.700
It was a dark evening, you know?

1015
00:46:48.860 --> 00:46:50.240
Oh, and you're hanging on every word.

1016
00:46:50.240 --> 00:46:54.940
Hanging on every word, and I have to share with you, this is a very actory moment.

1017
00:46:55.320 --> 00:46:56.760
I decided to do this.

1018
00:46:56.820 --> 00:47:03.220
No one told me that I made the choice that Angela Martin would literally be enthralled by

1019
00:47:03.220 --> 00:47:03.840
this man.

1020
00:47:04.940 --> 00:47:11.020
And so when Randall Einhorn was directing, he had Matt Soane, the camera operator, like pan

1021
00:47:11.020 --> 00:47:12.280
across all of our expressions.

1022
00:47:12.280 --> 00:47:16.200
And I had this expression of like, you know?

1023
00:47:16.440 --> 00:47:18.360
Oh, and you're loving it.

1024
00:47:18.440 --> 00:47:18.880
I'm loving it.

1025
00:47:18.880 --> 00:47:21.920
And Randall was like, Angela, that is so great.

1026
00:47:22.040 --> 00:47:23.400
Can you do that every time?

1027
00:47:23.540 --> 00:47:24.220
And I was like, oh, yeah.

1028
00:47:24.340 --> 00:47:24.620
Oh, yeah.

1029
00:47:24.760 --> 00:47:30.260
So that's my little actory choice, little nugget for you that I just thought that Angela Martin

1030
00:47:30.260 --> 00:47:31.420
would be enthralled.

1031
00:47:31.700 --> 00:47:36.520
Well, we had a very actory question for Andy Daly about this scene because we wanted to

1032
00:47:36.520 --> 00:47:42.520
know if he did any research on the character of Ben Franklin in order to play this role.

1033
00:47:43.520 --> 00:47:44.860
And here's what he had to say.

1034
00:47:45.060 --> 00:47:46.100
I did prepare a bit.

1035
00:47:46.200 --> 00:47:53.000
So as a office viewer, it always looked to me like the show was somewhat improvised.

1036
00:47:53.600 --> 00:47:58.900
I think it turns out, actually, that it's just really well written and really well acted

1037
00:47:58.900 --> 00:48:00.860
and not really so much improvised.

1038
00:48:00.860 --> 00:48:06.300
Of course, there is some improvising on the set, but not as much as I think I thought.

1039
00:48:06.300 --> 00:48:09.260
It looks so spontaneous on television.

1040
00:48:09.400 --> 00:48:17.700
But anyway, the point is that because I figured I would be improvising as a guy who impersonates

1041
00:48:17.700 --> 00:48:22.620
Ben Franklin for a living, I figured I better know quite a bit about Ben Franklin.

1042
00:48:22.620 --> 00:48:28.840
And so I just read Wikipedia, but I mean, I read it and I took notes and I kind of, you

1043
00:48:28.840 --> 00:48:33.680
know, I read it a few times to try to have a lot of this biographical information in my

1044
00:48:33.680 --> 00:48:34.240
mind.

1045
00:48:35.640 --> 00:48:42.000
And as I will address in a later answer to a later question, it came in handy.

1046
00:48:42.780 --> 00:48:44.400
But that is the preparation that I did.

1047
00:48:44.760 --> 00:48:45.640
I would do that.

1048
00:48:45.820 --> 00:48:50.240
We would go around about it differently, but we'd show up with information.

1049
00:48:51.060 --> 00:48:53.240
What does that mean, go around about it differently?

1050
00:48:53.460 --> 00:48:55.560
Well, it's just kind of like our research process.

1051
00:48:55.740 --> 00:48:58.860
You know, you always like, you look at my notes and you're like, oh, God, your notes

1052
00:48:58.860 --> 00:49:03.680
make me like queasy because I have like a gazillion Post-it notes and note cards and you have

1053
00:49:03.680 --> 00:49:05.260
like a very like outline.

1054
00:49:05.580 --> 00:49:05.920
Oh, yes.

1055
00:49:05.960 --> 00:49:06.120
Yeah.

1056
00:49:06.300 --> 00:49:07.240
I see what you're saying.

1057
00:49:07.440 --> 00:49:10.840
I would research Ben Franklin, write an essay on it and bring it with me.

1058
00:49:11.100 --> 00:49:16.720
You would fill your script with 72 Post-it notes filled with bits of information about

1059
00:49:16.720 --> 00:49:17.180
Ben Franklin.

1060
00:49:17.420 --> 00:49:17.540
Yes.

1061
00:49:19.240 --> 00:49:20.320
And there it is.

1062
00:49:20.740 --> 00:49:21.540
There it is.

1063
00:49:21.680 --> 00:49:22.980
I mean, the proof is right there.

1064
00:49:23.280 --> 00:49:26.160
You just held up your notes for this episode and it's like 72.

1065
00:49:26.420 --> 00:49:26.800
Post-it notes.

1066
00:49:27.320 --> 00:49:28.660
Post-it notes all around.

1067
00:49:28.980 --> 00:49:29.920
With arrows and highlighting.

1068
00:49:30.260 --> 00:49:35.240
Well, so listen, lady, before we get to Michael's man meat, should we take a break?

1069
00:49:36.500 --> 00:49:39.040
And then we'll come back and talk all about it.

1070
00:49:39.340 --> 00:49:41.860
That's the segue of the month.

1071
00:49:42.740 --> 00:49:45.000
It's definitely the segue for this episode.

1072
00:49:45.580 --> 00:49:46.760
We'll be back in a second.

1073
00:49:46.760 --> 00:49:56.630
Guys, we are back.

1074
00:49:56.910 --> 00:50:02.670
Michael is grilling steaks on his George Foreman grill down in the warehouse and Ryan

1075
00:50:02.670 --> 00:50:06.450
asks him, is it the same grill that he used to grill his foot?

1076
00:50:06.810 --> 00:50:08.130
And he's like, no.

1077
00:50:08.510 --> 00:50:09.230
Okay, yes.

1078
00:50:09.410 --> 00:50:10.630
But I got all the foot off.

1079
00:50:11.210 --> 00:50:11.550
Incredible.

1080
00:50:11.550 --> 00:50:20.530
Then we go upstairs and, whoa, Ben Franklin is tying a cherry stem with his tongue.

1081
00:50:20.810 --> 00:50:24.110
And Pam asks him what kind of undergarments he's wearing.

1082
00:50:24.110 --> 00:50:32.230
I just want to point out that Rashida's response as Karen to Ben Franklin tying that cherry stem is so perfect.

1083
00:50:32.570 --> 00:50:38.110
Because she's like, Ben Franklin did not just tie a cherry stem into a knot.

1084
00:50:38.310 --> 00:50:39.370
It's so good.

1085
00:50:39.610 --> 00:50:44.910
And then, yeah, Pam, when you ask him that, he has one of my favorite lines.

1086
00:50:45.850 --> 00:50:47.430
Andy is so good with this line.

1087
00:50:47.570 --> 00:50:50.170
He's like, you're very saucy.

1088
00:50:50.830 --> 00:50:54.170
Well, guys, we got a lot of fan questions about this scene.

1089
00:50:54.970 --> 00:51:02.930
Aaron, Brooke, Olivia, Laura, and Marie all wrote in to say, did Ben Franklin actually tie the cherry stem with his mouth?

1090
00:51:02.930 --> 00:51:05.350
And here is what Andy Daly had to say.

1091
00:51:06.170 --> 00:51:07.050
Absolutely not.

1092
00:51:07.050 --> 00:51:09.990
That is not something I've even ever tried to do.

1093
00:51:11.510 --> 00:51:12.310
That's crazy.

1094
00:51:12.490 --> 00:51:16.390
But I am struggling to remember how we shot it.

1095
00:51:16.510 --> 00:51:25.690
I guess I must have sort of stuck the tied cherry stem, sort of stashed it in the corner of my mouth, you know,

1096
00:51:25.830 --> 00:51:30.610
and then put the other one in and just kind of mimed it and then spit out.

1097
00:51:30.610 --> 00:51:32.230
But listen, that's hard, too,

1098
00:51:32.350 --> 00:51:42.790
to have a tied cherry stem hidden in your mouth and then put a real cherry stem in there that's not tied and then make sure you pull out the right one.

1099
00:51:43.110 --> 00:51:44.410
That's pretty impressive right there.

1100
00:51:44.490 --> 00:51:46.110
But I might be remembering it wrong.

1101
00:51:46.110 --> 00:51:53.310
It may actually be that the camera kind of swung off me long enough to not have to be so sneaky about it.

1102
00:51:53.830 --> 00:51:54.690
I don't remember.

1103
00:51:54.830 --> 00:52:00.250
But the short answer to your question is no, I did not really tie that cherry stem with my tongue.

1104
00:52:00.790 --> 00:52:07.950
I can't imagine how one does that or why one would take the time and effort to learn how.

1105
00:52:08.230 --> 00:52:10.970
I mean, I know why people do that.

1106
00:52:11.210 --> 00:52:14.230
Is it like a look what my tongue can do kind of thing?

1107
00:52:14.490 --> 00:52:14.770
Yeah.

1108
00:52:15.090 --> 00:52:18.370
It's a display of your tongue agility.

1109
00:52:18.670 --> 00:52:19.730
It's like a sexual thing.

1110
00:52:19.730 --> 00:52:20.890
Why did you say it with such authority?

1111
00:52:21.150 --> 00:52:22.310
Hey, I know.

1112
00:52:22.670 --> 00:52:24.050
I know why people do that.

1113
00:52:24.770 --> 00:52:28.910
Well, people want to know if either of us can tie a cherry stem with our mouths.

1114
00:52:28.910 --> 00:52:31.210
It's a little bit of an inappropriate question.

1115
