Ben Franklin slash Gordon basically says, I don't think she needs to know this information.

1396
01:06:30.630 --> 01:06:34.730
And Michael is like, Ben Franklin, you're kind of a sleazebag.

1397
01:06:35.030 --> 01:06:38.650
And you guys, Ben Franklin was kind of a sleazebag with women.

1398
01:06:38.910 --> 01:06:40.370
He like actually really was.

1399
01:06:40.530 --> 01:06:47.470
If you look it up, he just he like literally slept with so many women.

1400
01:06:47.470 --> 01:06:51.110
And there's one thing that's inaccurate in this episode, though.

1401
01:06:51.390 --> 01:06:56.450
In this episode, you know, he had a child with one woman who was not his wife.

1402
01:06:56.830 --> 01:07:02.330
And in the episode, he says that, like, she didn't know.

1403
01:07:03.210 --> 01:07:09.810
That he had he sort of says to Michael, like, I fathered a child and I never told my wife about it.

1404
01:07:09.890 --> 01:07:11.230
But that's not true.

1405
01:07:11.510 --> 01:07:14.690
Actually, his wife raised that child like her own.

1406
01:07:14.690 --> 01:07:15.870
Oh, my gosh.

1407
01:07:16.450 --> 01:07:19.910
His wife, Deborah, was a saint, I'm going to say.

1408
01:07:19.910 --> 01:07:22.330
And she put up with Ben's bad behavior.

1409
01:07:22.330 --> 01:07:27.550
Well, now Michael did not like his advice from Ben Franklin.

1410
01:07:27.550 --> 01:07:31.230
So he's going to go ask Elizabeth for her advice instead.

1411
01:07:31.610 --> 01:07:33.150
Here is her advice to Michael.

1412
01:07:33.430 --> 01:07:37.210
Quote, secrets, secrets are no fun.

1413
01:07:38.290 --> 01:07:40.850
Secrets, secrets hurt someone.

1414
01:07:43.260 --> 01:07:44.720
Angela, do you know what that is?

1415
01:07:44.860 --> 01:07:45.600
Do you know what that quote is?

1416
01:07:45.780 --> 01:07:48.560
Please tell me you researched this quote.

1417
01:07:48.680 --> 01:07:50.120
Is it from like a children's book?

1418
01:07:50.280 --> 01:07:50.860
What is it from?

1419
01:07:50.860 --> 01:08:01.700
These are the opening lyrics to a song called No Secrets by a girl band called No Secrets from their album.

1420
01:08:01.700 --> 01:08:02.260
No Secrets?

1421
01:08:02.380 --> 01:08:03.320
No Secrets.

1422
01:08:04.300 --> 01:08:06.860
And I asked Sam and Cody to pull a clip.

1423
01:08:07.000 --> 01:08:07.580
Here it is, Angela.

1424
01:08:09.420 --> 01:08:13.840
Secrets, secrets are no fun.

1425
01:08:15.780 --> 01:08:19.500
Secrets, secrets hurt someone.

1426
01:08:33.960 --> 01:08:37.140
No Secrets was a British-American girl band.

1427
01:08:37.140 --> 01:08:38.980
Very reminiscent of Spice Girls.

1428
01:08:39.280 --> 01:08:45.100
They had one hit, which was a cover of Kids in America, that song by Kim Wilde.

1429
01:08:45.460 --> 01:08:47.260
We're the kids in America.

1430
01:08:47.600 --> 01:08:49.780
Oh, we're the kids in America.

1431
01:08:50.080 --> 01:08:50.860
Do you remember that song?

1432
01:08:50.960 --> 01:08:51.600
I kind of do.

1433
01:08:51.840 --> 01:08:57.100
They followed up with another hit single, That's What Girls Do, but they only ever made one album.

1434
01:08:57.940 --> 01:09:00.640
They started on a second one, but it was never released.

1435
01:09:00.640 --> 01:09:06.700
The band broke up over disagreements, and one member claims it was parent drama and interference.

1436
01:09:07.260 --> 01:09:09.260
But I, here's the thing.

1437
01:09:09.640 --> 01:09:11.920
Mindy Kaling wrote this episode.

1438
01:09:12.480 --> 01:09:21.500
I have no doubt, no doubt in my mind that she has the album No Secrets by No Secrets, and that's how she knew to quote this line.

1439
01:09:21.500 --> 01:09:23.240
I mean, it seems pretty specific.

1440
01:09:23.600 --> 01:09:33.820
We also had a fan catch in this scene from Corinna Liu, who says at 17 minutes, 52 seconds, there is a flyer on the refrigerator behind Michael for silver on spruce.

1441
01:09:34.260 --> 01:09:42.440
Corinna says, I did a small deep dive, and it looks like this is a real business with two different addresses, and the telephone number on the flyer is correct.

1442
01:09:43.540 --> 01:09:44.800
I checked it out.

1443
01:09:45.020 --> 01:09:46.060
Corinna is right.

1444
01:09:46.520 --> 01:09:48.080
Yes, silver on spruce.

1445
01:09:48.320 --> 01:09:54.240
I wonder if this jewelry store has gotten, like, prank calls because you can see the phone number in our episode.

1446
01:09:55.140 --> 01:09:58.400
Well, I imagine Corinna is not the first person to freeze frame on this.

1447
01:09:58.400 --> 01:10:01.300
I wonder if the kids on the talk have called the number.

1448
01:10:01.640 --> 01:10:05.600
Lady, it is not called the talk, and you're not going to get them to call at the talk.

1449
01:10:06.360 --> 01:10:06.840
Okay?

1450
01:10:07.160 --> 01:10:08.940
Gosh, everyone on the talk.

1451
01:10:09.700 --> 01:10:14.680
All right, guys, we're almost done, I promise, I promise,

1452
01:10:14.700 --> 01:10:30.860
but we cannot leave this episode without talking about this scene where Dwight is interrogating Ben Franklin because Jim has convinced him that this is the real Ben Franklin who has time-traveled to visit us at Dunder Mifflin.

1453
01:10:30.920 --> 01:10:38.240
He's 99% sure it's not the real Ben Franklin, but he's going to interrogate him anyway.

1454
01:10:38.240 --> 01:10:39.880
Yeah, the scene was so funny.

1455
01:10:41.000 --> 01:10:41.880
So funny.

1456
01:10:42.080 --> 01:10:47.700
And Dwight is just, like, challenging him with questions about the time period when he lived.

1457
01:10:47.900 --> 01:10:53.840
And Andy told us that this was one of his favorite to shoot, and this is what he had to say.

1458
01:10:53.840 --> 01:10:59.040
This is where my research into Ben Franklin came in handy.

1459
01:10:59.820 --> 01:11:08.880
There were a bunch of scripted lines in that scene where Rainn Wilson is challenging this Ben Franklin impersonator,

1460
01:11:09.020 --> 01:11:14.100
trying to trip him up to find the lapse in his knowledge about Ben Franklin.

1461
01:11:14.100 --> 01:11:17.120
And so he's just throwing all these questions.

1462
01:11:17.340 --> 01:11:22.940
But one that he improvised was, are you nearsighted or farsighted?

1463
01:11:23.040 --> 01:11:24.500
That was not in the script.

1464
01:11:24.500 --> 01:11:27.460
It was never discussed beforehand that he was going to say that.

1465
01:11:27.620 --> 01:11:30.860
He just threw that out in the middle of a take.

1466
01:11:30.860 --> 01:11:38.580
And I, because I had just read the Wikipedia page about Ben Franklin, knew that Ben Franklin invented the bifocals.

1467
01:11:38.580 --> 01:11:47.100
And he invented the bifocals because he needed them, because his distance sight was challenged, as was his reading sight.

1468
01:11:47.100 --> 01:11:52.080
And so I was able to say, without having to think about it or hesitate, both.

1469
01:11:52.520 --> 01:11:54.680
That's why I invented the bifocal.

1470
01:11:55.320 --> 01:12:02.060
And that is an unusual, kind of magical, improvised moment.

1471
01:12:02.060 --> 01:12:09.020
It's so strange that he asked me a question for which I was prepared with the perfect answer.

1472
01:12:09.260 --> 01:12:10.540
It's very strange.

1473
01:12:10.720 --> 01:12:14.340
And in fact, when they called Cut, I remember Mindy Kaling saying,

1474
01:12:14.340 --> 01:12:16.080
did you guys work that out beforehand?

1475
01:12:16.260 --> 01:12:17.160
And we were both like, no.

1476
01:12:17.320 --> 01:12:19.620
And we were all kind of stumped.

1477
01:12:19.920 --> 01:12:22.540
That's, it's very strange that that's an improvised moment.

1478
01:12:23.760 --> 01:12:27.080
And yeah, it ended up in the show, of course, because why, why wouldn't it?

1479
01:12:28.160 --> 01:12:29.800
So yes, that's my answer.

1480
01:12:30.880 --> 01:12:31.280
Amazing.

1481
01:12:31.460 --> 01:12:35.200
Lady, this is, you know, my nerdy moment where I say it's the group mind.

1482
01:12:35.580 --> 01:12:38.280
Also, actors, this is why you need to do your prep work.

